{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/yz61e3","slideIndex":3,"text":"Evidence snapshot 24 October 2026, 20:55 UTC. These are deterministic implementation rules, not calibrated physiological thresholds or a measurement of rep-count accuracy. RepCounter requires confidence>=0.6 and a complete top-bottom-top cycle, resets on gaps>0.75s or nonmonotonic time, uses0.15s zone stability and accepts0.6–15s cycle duration. CoachingPolicy compares a new valid rep with at least five prior valid durations using mean+max(sampleSD,0.25s). Discomfort stops coaching; lifecycle invalidation prevents old cues/sensor callbacks entering a new state. Sources: /Users/scsoc/dev/AI PT/Shared/Core/RepCounter.swift; /Users/scsoc/dev/AI PT/Shared/Core/CoachingPolicy.swift; /Users/scsoc/dev/AI PT/docs/watch-telemetry.md; /Users/scsoc/dev/AI PT/docs/voice-feedback.md. Phase images are existing illustrations, not captured workout evidence."}
